>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be numeric: int, float, or complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (when out is provided, its shape must match input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (out dtype must be float for real inputs and complex for complex inputs — prevents casting to Short)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 then 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8 else if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8 else 9 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 4 (for float or complex inputs, out dtype must equal input dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 then dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1) else if 9 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10 then dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
